{title: Blessed Assurance}
{lyricist: Fanny J. Crosby, 1873}
{composer: ASSURANCE, Phoebe P. Knapp, 1873}
{copyright: Public domain}
{key: D}
{time: 9/8}
{tempo: 60}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Blessed as[D7]surance, [G]Jesus is [D]mine!
O what a [A]foretaste of [E7]glory di[A]vine!
[D]Heir of sal[D7]vation, [G]purchase of [D]God,
[G]Born of His [D]Spirit, [A]washed in His [D]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]This is my story, [G]this is my [D]song,
Praising my Savior [A]all the day long;
[D]This is my story, [G]this is my [D]song,
[G]Praising my [D]Savior [A]all the day [D]long.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Perfect sub[D7]mission, [G]perfect de[D]light,
Visions of [A]rapture now [E7]burst on my [A]sight;
[D]Angels de[D7]scending bring [G]from a[D]bove
[G]Echoes of [D]mercy, [A]whispers of [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Perfect sub[D7]mission, [G]all is at [D]rest,
I in my [A]Savior am [E7]happy and [A]blest,
[D]Watching and [D7]waiting, [G]looking a[D]bove,
[G]Filled with His [D]goodness, [A]lost in His [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
